  "question": {
    "text": "Niobium ( Nb ) and ruthenium $(\\mathrm{Ru})$ have \" $x$ \" and \" $y$ \" number of electrons in their respective 4 d orbitals. The value of $x+y$ is ______ -.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "11",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{Z}=41 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Nb} \\text { (Niobium) : }[\\mathrm{Kr}]_{36} 4 \\mathrm{~d}^4 5 \\mathrm{~s}^1 \\\\ & \\text { Number of electron in } 4 \\mathrm{~d}=4=\\mathrm{x} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Z}=44 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Ru} \\text { (Ruthenium) }[\\mathrm{Kr}]_{36} 4 \\mathrm{~d}^7 5 \\mathrm{~s}^1 \\\\ & \\text { Number of electron in } 4 \\mathrm{~d}=7=\\mathrm{y} \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}=11\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
